  "limitations": [
    "These conclusions compare with a freshly measured frozen copy of the retained one-range GET, not the rejected full-run DB-reference experiment.",
    "Only one application file differs, and its changes affect GET response encoding. No migration, storage-format, POST-write, client-lifetime or S3-read change.",
    "Repeated benchmark results support the large-GET improvement in this local in-process setup; they are not production p95 or concurrent throughput measurements.",
    "Cold CPU includes profiler overhead; removing many recursive calls can make the profiled percentage larger than the unprofiled latency percentage.",
    "Memray captures whole test functions, not server RSS. Single-capture fluctuations do not prove a per-request RAM improvement.",
    "Raw benchmark Git metadata identifies the checkout, not the uncommitted candidate. Frozen before/after source snapshots and application SHA-256 fingerprints identify the measured code.",
    "The benchmark tab displays the first completed after-run, selected by collection order. The other five suites remain archived; the 10.6% conclusion uses all three before and all three after reports."
